If ENVIRONMENT=dev, then use the dev config with local PostgreSQL
If ENVIRONMENT=prod, then use the prod config with Google Cloud SQL
All SQL queries should be compatible with PostgreSQL
Follow refactoring best practices, especially DRY, Single Responsibility, Singleton, and YAGNI
Prefer hard failures over silent failures, don't set defaults except in exceptional cases where it makes a lot of sense.
Database update failures should always stop the program because otherwise users are using our tokens for free.
You can always restart the server without asking for permission.
Use Pydantic models to validate data.

# Async Best Practices
Always use async/await consistently throughout the entire call chain - never mix sync operations (like next()) with async contexts
Handle all response types explicitly (dict, str, AsyncGenerator) with proper type checking and conversion fallbacks
Use proper error recovery in streaming contexts - catch errors but maintain the stream where possible
Ensure all async generators properly yield [DONE] messages to close streams